2	// plan-before-generation ordering (stage file Step 2-4).
3	//
4	// The stage prose says generation never begins before the human answers
5	// "Approve Plan": the conductor writes code-generation-plan.md, presents the
6	// Plan Approval question through code-generation-questions.md, and only an
7	// explicit approval authorizes the developer-agent dispatch. A field report
8	// showed prose losing that contest: a conductor generated the code first and
9	// backfilled the plan beside code-summary.md, making the plan an output
10	// instead of the input. The stage-completion artifact guard cannot catch
11	// this - it fires at completion time, when the backfilled plan already
12	// exists. Per the framework layering (determinism belongs in tools and
13	// hooks, knowledge in agents, judgement with humans), this hook is the
14	// ordering's deterministic twin.
15	//
16	// This is one of the framework's flow-altering hooks. Its contract is the
17	// harness-native PreToolUse block: print a reason to stderr and exit 2 to
18	// refuse the tool call, exit 0 to allow. The refusal is scoped tightly to
19	// code-generation: developer-agent dispatch and workspace mutation are both
20	// blocked until the same approval evidence is current. Writes inside the
21	// selected code-generation record dir remain available to create the plan,
22	// instructions, questions, and diary that make approval possible.
23	//
24	// How the hook decides: the active directive is the approval authority. A
25	// directive with `unit` selects construction/<unit>/code-generation; a
26	// zero-Unit directive selects construction/code-generation. Step 4 dispatches
27	// carry that choice explicitly as `AIDLC-UNIT: <unit>` or
28	// `AIDLC-STAGE: code-generation`, plus the exact `AIDLC-TESTING-CONTRACT`
29	// marker. The selected target must have a non-empty plan and test instructions,
30	// a structured contract matching current memory/scope/strategy/type, an
31	// explicit "Approve Plan" answer, and a matching approval fingerprint over
32	// those exact bytes. Missing, conflicting, unknown, stale, and
33	// post-approval-modified evidence blocks instead of guessing.
34	//
35	// Fail-open outside code-generation: a missing or unreadable state file, an
36	// active directive/current stage other than code-generation, malformed stdin,
37	// an unknown/read-only tool, a non-developer subagent target, or any throw
38	// allows the call. Once a code-generation generation path is identified,
39	// missing or ambiguous target evidence blocks. The deterministic off-switch
40	// AIDLC_DISABLE_PLAN_APPROVAL_GUARD=1 disables enforcement entirely (the
41	// documented escape hatch for false-positive storms, mirroring the
42	// reviewer-scope guard's off-switch). Every genuine block emits a
43	// PLAN_APPROVAL_BLOCKED audit event so the run's record shows when the ordering
